Welcome crawlers to the eighth dungeon crawler Carl book recap where I'll be covering a parade of horribles chapter by chapter. And do not worry, there are no spoilers outside of what happens in this book. And while 
this is the final recap in this series until we get book nine, I have a lot more dungeon crawler Carl content in the works, including a recap of the extra pineapple cabaret chapters, as well as tons of lore videos as 
well. So, make sure to like and subscribe to Mana and Toast if all that sounds good to you. That said, let's get this thing started. Donut's new lawyer, Princess Chandra, conducts an outreach guild interview with Donut 
from a damaged Naga battle cruiser. She helped overthrow the Naga king and put her uncle in power. And now she wants to make enough money to leave for the center system. Chandra is the widow of Rishi, whom Carl killed 
in the previous book. And because of this, she can claim widow's rights, allowing her to choose to marry her husband's killer without his consent. She has used that right to marry Carl and claim his earnings. The 
faction wars prize money has already gone into her trust and Shandra has also hired assassins to kill Quaazar. Now during the interview, Donut makes sure the audience can see the marriage certificate, court orders, and 
banking records. Donut then offers 50 million credits to anyone who stops Chandra and her family with another 10 million for the head that she could display. Carl reaches the 10th floor with 5,51 crawlers remaining as 
most of the crawlers who survived faction wars have already taken exit deals. Quazar reports that Scolopendra is awake and moving and just its lights trap connected the nothing shaw the halls of ascendancy in 
Scolapendra's layer releasing creatures that are now attacking guests on the 18th floor. Those guests are trying to reach the safety of the 16th floor but first they have to survive the 17th. Now, Donut chooses a new 
class called Assassin of Skeut, which gives her a healing aura and magical pet hats that provide extra protection and other buffs for and Rend. At the garage, they meet two gremlins, Hedi, who handles mechanical 
weapons, and Waldrip Chris, who trains living mounts. The type of vehicle they choose will determine which attendant stays with them. Donut chooses a mechanical vehicle, leaving Hedi as their garage attendant. Carl and 
Donuts then spin a prize wheel to find out which vehicle they'll get. It lands on a food truck with a big shot chicken logo styled to look like a prohibition era car. A giant plastic Tommy gun sits on the front 
partially blocking the windshield. Cascadia begins the announcement sounding distressed as she tells the remaining crawlers they should have taken exit deals. Zev then takes over to explain the floor's rules. Roughly 
1,800 teams will compete in seven races called heats over seven days. At least one team will be eliminated from each heat. Normally, that's the team that will come and last. But if another team dies or fails to finish, 
the remaining teams can all advance. Each team that completes a heat earns a vehicle upgrade, while the winner gets to choose between three regular upgrades or one golden upgrade. Zev also explains that teams can attack 
other vehicles, but cannot steal them. They also must change drivers between heats since the same person cannot drive two races in a row. The first race is a 53 km course through the caves of the screeching death 
manatees with 6 hours given to finish. Perpetente suspects that if too many NPC teams are eliminated, crawler teams will be brought in to replace them, forcing friends to race against one another. Ammani suggests 
keeping the other NPC teams alive whenever possible, and Carl agrees. At the cave entrance, a bug bear runs from a burning minivan, blocking the road. Nearby, an enormous manatee crushes another team's giant ladybug 
mount. That mount's death causes its riders to explode, eliminating their team. Donut kills the manatee, attacking the bug bears. The manatee's description links it to a world turned into an adventure park and says one 
of the people responsible for that park is now staying at Club Scolopendra. Now, rather than take the experience points for the kill, Donut chooses an audience vote that will either send the manity or someone 
representing it into the 11th floor arena. Now, Carl stops to help Ratoslav and Yasha, the two surviving bug bears, from team freelo. Their third teammate died when their minivan crashed. They remember earlier lives of 
theirs in the dungeon and the cold place where they waited between them. A voice offered them a choice. return to that cold or enter the races for a chance to win a real home. Although their damaged minivan can no 
longer run, the system still counts it as a vehicle, so their team has not yet been eliminated. Carl offers to tow it across the finish line. Now, as they travel, team Sparkles overtakes them on a mount made of living 
vines called an avernous creeper. Its riders are unicorn named Dwight and a ratlike mandigot called Lucine. They insult Carl and Donut before their mount fires thorns as it pushes past. And Carl collects some of those 
thorns after learning that each one can grow into an invasive plant, although they won't be able to sprout on this floor. And Carl and Donut reach Hungry Eyes Village with the minivan and tow. And Rotolav thanks them 
for saving his team. Carl and Donut finish in seventh with team Free Love coming in eighth. And although the Bug Bears finish last, they survive because the manatee already eliminated the team riding the ladybug mount. 
Then Carl and Donut get a preview of the second heat. They'll be assigned to one of two 10 kmter routes, each with a boss that he must defeat before finishing. Because Carl drove in the first heat, somebody else must 
drive in the second. And they initially plan for Donut to take over. Hedi suggests that Carl build controls suited to Donut instead of spending an official upgrade on them. Ordinary modifications are allowed between 
races, but magical improvements must come through the racing system and rewards. Now, for their vehicle upgrade, they choose retractable spider legs, allowing the truck to climb walls, but it'll slow down while 
deployed. Hedi considers the legs important because only the first three heats are guaranteed to have paved roads. We see Morai, who takes the form of a shadow mimic on this floor, allowing him to imitate other 
creatures. And in the safe room, he appears as a moonreaper, a creature whose gaze can trap people in frightening visions that seem to last much longer than the encounter itself. Biggs the slugalo says Morai told her 
that she would drown in fire. Splash zone also experienced a frightening vision involving his own family. Morai says these threats and visions are meant to hurt and frighten people and warns them against treating the 
experiences as reliable predictions. Rosetta suggests keeping new visitors away from him until they understand what triggers his transformations. Carl learns a new spell called Uzi form, which temporarily turns him into 
slime so he can slip through small openings. Donut's new assassin class gives her smoke form, a spell that lets her turn into smoke. It also gives her a healing aura called healer's grasp. Separately, the class 
strengthens the plant and vermin spells she's already gained through her previous class, Oakfell. Now, Donut's new class also provides protective headgear for and Ren. And once per day, if Donut's health falls below 
10%, either pet wearing its headgear within three meters of her becomes invulnerable for a minute. And during that time, Mongo's strength will double and Ren will gain the ability to heal a party member. Ren's headband 
also gives his bites another effect. If he kills a creature with a bite, there's a chance its corpse will be raised as an undead servant. Now, among Donuts rewards are emergency gremlin scrolls, which summon a gremlin 
to repair a broken down vehicle or heal a living mount during a race. She also receives Danforth crossbow bolts, which lock whatever part of a target they strike into place. Donut also receives the crerer of the 
benevant champion and an edible figure shaped like the god Meetus, which she then eats. Now, eating the meat figure transforms Donut's claws, which now glow blue and are powerful enough to slice straight through the 
safe room table. Morai explains that her new claws can cut ghosts as well as physical objects. And this ability will also carry over to her astral paw ability, the spell she uses to create a magical paw that can reach 
things from a distance. The downside is that the change is permanent and Donut cannot turn the effect off. Although retracting her claws will keep her from accidentally cutting everything she touches. One of Donut's 
reward boxes also contain a spell book which she uses to learn ice slick, a spell that lets her cover an area in ice. Carl receives a potion that adds more quick access inventory slots and a baby backpack for carrying 
Donut on his chest. With Donut buckled in, he should be able to use Uzi form to turn them both into slime or bring her along when he phases through an obstacle. Though they need to test it first. Now Carl then opens a 
fan box containing belongings he inherited from Rishi through his marriage to Chandra. Broken furniture, damaged appliances, and rubbish all spill out onto the room, and Carl's begins to search the pile for anything 
useful. Carl takes a second cleaner bot out of his inventory to help clear away Rishi's belongings, but it immediately shrieks and tries to wrigle free. Morai resets the bot, an old model once used to clean architect 
Houston's operating room. Now, back in the garage, Carl and Donut find Hedi and the other Gremlins taking their truck apart to repair damage and install upgrades. Carl and Donut leave their garage to meet the other 
racers in the team roundabout. Safe room rules apply here so the teams cannot attack each other. They find Ratoslav and Yasha, the bug bears they rescued, who show them a magical cooler they received as a reward, which 
never seems to run out of peach beer. Three ninjas from another racing team called the Wild Hunt emerge from their garage. Their leader is Chiomi, a razor fox with an enchanted helmet that lets her assess the abilities 
of people nearby. Genesis and Rapture also emerge from their garage. These are two Lady Manitars belonging to a racing team called Lady Dominators and the Chiomi warns Carl and Donut about their domination magic, which 
can drain energy or mana. But Morai thinks Carl's mind balance, and Donut's high charisma will likely protect them. The Lady Dominator's third teammate has been split down the middle, leaving only the right half of his 
body, which is magically being kept alive. Now, Donut recognizes him as Dong Kyot's missing partner, Corkunda, also known as Corki. Carl then receives a quest to reunite Dong with Corki, find Corkunda's other half, 
Porky, and get a fleshmaner to put the two halves back together. Carl and Donut then enter Hungry Eyes Vendor Village, where the main square has no safe room protection. Other areas are protected from attacks, but 
poisoning is allowed everywhere in the village. They also cannot inspect the food to check what it contains. And they find Propetente arguing with his racing teammate Jurgen, a general from Faction Wars who has ignored 
Prepente's warnings about the street food and is now throwing up. The two ride Sweetie, a giant pig-like animal in the races, but Prepotente fears Jurgens's insistence on trusting his instincts will get them killed in 
the next heat. Jurgen also talks to his absent wife, Heidi, as though she were there standing beside him. Now, Carl and Donut join their friends at the Lollipop karaoke bar where Ellie is being pestered by a fan named 
Lionus. He has paid to visit her in the dungeon through her show contract, which allows him to stay even though she wants him to leave her alone. Floren, who has teamed up with Lucia Maher, has hired extra help to take 
Lucia's turn driving because her personality has been changing unpredictably since her dogs died. He still doesn't know why she stayed in the dungeon after promising to take an exit deal. Ammani reports that Lina, who 
is racing with Zen, killed every other team in their first race. This could force them to face other crawlers in the next heat as replacements for the teams they've killed. Louiesie, Britney, and Bautista's racing 
vehicle is a low rider that sits so close to the ground that it keeps scraping along the track. They finished second to last and survived only because another team had been eliminated. As the last surviving team to 
finish, they had to let the audience choose their upgrade and received glowing wheel spinners instead of something useful. Now feeling lonely, Propetente asks Carl and Donut about using an enchanted pet biscuit on 
another goat who was his girlfriend back when he was an ordinary goat. He has three of these biscuits, each with different effects. One would turn her into an intelligent, upright level one crawler and permanently charm 
her into loving him. Another would make her a crawler but keep her original body without forcing her to fall in love. And the third would turn her into a dungeon pet that could gain levels and abilities. Donut tells 
Prepente he should not use magic to make someone love him and warns him that she would be in terrible danger as a level one crawler on this floor. Donut offers to talk to Prepente every day instead and he leaves the 
biscuits unused. Bucket Boy, the crocodilian NPC who was rescued on the previous floor, volunteers to drive Carl and Donut during the second race. So Carl teaches him to use the truck's controls and retractable spider 
legs. Hetti has also made controls that Dona can operate if she needs to take over. Carl tries to remove the giant plastic Tommy gun blocking the windshield, but the system won't allow it. The truck's navigation system 
speaks in the voice of Dr. Metalf Bee's former therapist, while Donut discovers that the freezer they have automatically replaces any food they take out. Now, just before the race, Zang reports that the replacement for 
the five teams Lena killed include two crawler teams, one of which belongs to Tran. So, Lea and Zang will now have to race against him. Carl and Donut prepare an attack on the Lady Dominator's team with help from Chiomi 
and the Bug Bears. Donut will use Katya's crossbow to shoot their driver, Rapture, with a Daneforth bolt that will hold her in place while Chiomi's giant bear rams the car. Carl shatters their truck's windshield to give 
Donut a clear shot at Rapture. Though nearby, Team Sparkles argues with another team of slimelike guck elementals and then destroys the elementals vehicle with a cannon before Donut can do her attack. So Carl calls off 
Donut's shots to avoid an additional elimination, which could bring replacement crawler teams into their next race. As Bucket Boy drives through the hail that is coming down, Donut uses her shield spell to cover the 
truck. They catch up with the Lady Dominators and another racing team called One Fine Pig, whose armored vehicle also has a protective shield. Its members are two Tigrins, Nico and Daario, and an ordinary Yorkshshire 
pig named Penelopey. When Carl examines Penelopey, her system description explains that a curse makes certain NPCs fall in love with her, including both Tigrins and the thunder god Tyrannis. Tyrannis protects her so 
that anyone that hurts Penelope will be marked for death by him. The racers are then blocked by two giant kangaroo like bosses. They cannot pass the boss ahead of them unless it is defeated. So the teams near Carl 
agreed to work together. The boss's descriptions explain that their young died because they could not protect them from the constant storms. They are now grabbing other creatures to replace the joeies in their pouches. 
But the pouches secrete an oil that burns the skin of other species. A razor fox from Chiomi's team attacks the boss from inside its pouch, but the boss ends up eating him and restoring all of its health. Chiomi then 
tells Carl that the pouch seems to be its only weak spot. And Carl then asked Donut to examine the dead Joey's, and she discovers that their skins can be collected, giving him the idea of wearing one to protect himself 
from the oil while attacking from inside. Carl then summons eight emergency gremlins to distract the kangaroo boss and summons Gunter and has Pontiff, one fine pig's hired driver, strike him with a mallet. Gunter then 
carries a force of that blow to the boss, knocking it down when it reaches it. Genesis, one of the lady dominators, is supposed to retrieve a dead Joey for Carl, but her grappling hook hits and kills a trapped upgrade 
engineer instead. Carl takes the enchanted Joey skin the engineer was wearing and puts it on to protect himself from the burning oil. The costume forces him to hop and makes his hands difficult to use while leaving his 
face exposed. He jumps into the boss's pouch, plants explosives, and escapes with his gloom wraith phase ability as the blast kills the boss. However, he discovers that he cannot remove the Joey skin costume until its 
12-hour timer runs out. Team Sparkles ends up winning the race while Carl and Donut finish last among the surviving teams. The next race will begin in eight hours, so Carl will still be wearing the Joey costume during 
it. The course will run 30 km downhill through waves of enemies with only 20 minutes to finish. Because Carl and Donut came in last among the surviving teams, the audience will choose their upgrade, and they choose a 
princess throne that Hedi says will help protect Donut. Meanwhile, Bucket Boy tells Dong that they have found Corki on the Nether Racing team. Learning this, Dong rushes to the Lady Dominator's garage. Carl struggles to 
catch up to him with his kangaroo costume on. He's worried that Dong will go inside where safe room rules cannot protect him. Zev then announces the teams must make a media appearance between races and books Carl and 
Donut for an interview on Plenty of Plenty. She also reads an AI announcement that the 11th floor is called a parade of horribles where the surviving crawlers will join a parade leading to an arena. The AI also claims 
as intercepted a Valt bomb capable of destroying the entire solar system and redirected it to an undisclosed location. Carl's escape plan skill reveals a hidden message in a drawing on the invoice from a vehicle 
modification shop. The message is from Akuma, one of the war mages from the faction wars, who tells Carl to eliminate two teams in the next race, and then to come to the shop alone afterward for an explanation. Akuma 
claims he can smuggle Carl's friends to the Pineapple Cabaret and help them escape the dungeon. Now, Carl eventually catches up to Dong and finds him on his hands and knees outside the Lady Dominator's garage, saying he 
feels sick while Genesis and Rapture mock him from behind the closed door. Corki calls back to Dong from inside and hearing each other is enough to complete the first part of Carl's reunion quest. The quest description 
explains that Corki is the half of Corkunda who stayed a dancer and fell in love with Dong, while the Porky half became a singer and dislikes him. A fleshmaner can reunite the two halves and free Corkunda from his 
obligation to race for the Lady Dominators, but it is unclear which personality will remain. Completing the quest will let Carl choose any two people within the AI's reach to bring into the 11th floor arena, though it 
will fail if Dong dies. Now, back in the garage, Ammani notices that Dong's health is not recovering despite being healed. He left his sock full of nickels behind when he rushed to see Corki, and she suspects that being 
away from it is what made him sick. Returning the sock to him seems to be keeping him alive without restoring his health. For now, they decide to keep Dong near the sock and out of the races. Carl then drinks a platinum 
hot list expansion potion, which adds more quick access inventory slots and unlocks a feature called contingency. This allows him to set actions to happen automatically when the conditions he chooses are met. is 
supposed to be guarding Hedi in the garage, but he wanders into the safe room with Ren following him. Morai then enters in his Reaper form, rises into the air, and turns towards Rend. In a deep voice, he warns Ren that 
he will die again. And Rend immediately drops dead. Now, Reaper gaze was one of Ren's weaknesses, which is why Moreai's ability killed him instantly. But Ren revives for the sixth time with his memories intact and 
becomes 25% stronger. This resurrection also gives him a new weakness, potatoes. With Morcai in the safe room and an endless supply of fries in the truck, Carl decides to keep Ren in his pet carrier except when they are 
fighting. Ammani suggests the guild's pet stables as another place where he can safely get some exercise. Rosetta and Tippid then return with two newly hired mercenaries and news that they may have found a fleshmaner 
capable of putting Cunda back together. They also have a lead on where Porky may be working as a singer. Now Carl and Donut are then teleported to a production facility at the bottom of the ocean for their appearance on 
Plenty of Plenty, a show run by the Plenty, the goatleike capids who sponsor Carl. Now Lexus, who normally hosts after hours, meets them to help prepare for the interview. Her own show is on hold and she is temporarily 
working for Borrent while she is unable to leave the solar system. Lexus explains that the open intelligent action network, the resistance group led by former crawler and cookbook author Porthus, sees the ships orbiting 
Earth after faction wars. With the showrunners communications disrupted, Zev is struggling to keep the crawls broadcast running and has brought in Lexus to help. When Donut asks about Katya, Lexus says they have been in 
contact with her, but Katya and the others have not returned to the children's facility in South Asia. An unidentified entity is protecting the facility in their absence. Lexus starts to describe seeing Katya the day 
before, but stops mid-sentence after her tablet beeps and turns the conversation back to the upcoming interview. Now, during the Plenty interview, the Caprid panelists question Carl and Donut and let them ask questions 
in return. Carl asks what Justice Light did at the end of Faction Wars, and a panelist named Baan explains that he broke open the dungeons nothing, releasing its inhabitants onto other floors. Carl discovers that Baan 
is one of the chief engineers of the Plenty's tunnel network, which connects star systems across the galaxy. Carl then receives urgent messages from Orin, the syndicate liaison, and Prime Minister Victory. They tell him 
the AI's influence has spread beyond Earth's solar system, and dungeon gods are appearing near tunnel connections in other systems. Orin explains that the system used to control gods without sponsors has been turned 
off, leaving them free to act on their own. Orin and Victory have been unable to reach the Plenty's leadership, but the Caprids Carl is interviewing are the very people they need to speak to. Orin gives Carl a carefully 
worded question to ask about the tunnels. Instead, Carl asks the panel whether the public knows that gods have escaped the dungeon and that the AI's enhancement zones have spread into the tunnel network. He warns the 
audience that they are in danger and need to run. Victory confirms that the warning went out live and that the AI allowed it to be broadcast. Carl's warning sends the Caprid panel into a panic. They believe the escaped 
gods signal a coming judgment by the Epicure, the god they worship, and most abandon the interview. Gamori, the plenty's matriarch and lead tunnel engineer, admits she kept the news from the herd because she feared 
exactly this reaction. Carl objects to being blamed when nobody had told him what was happening either. Harbinger, the Caprid liaison who monitored Carl's earlier sponsor interviews, appears in the studio and reveals 
that Gamori is his mother. He accuses her of ignoring his warnings after he recognized residual activity in the dungeon and realized how unstable the AI had become. Gamori orders him to leave, but he pulls a gun on Carl 
while insisting he was the one trying to protect everyone. Before Harbinger can fire, the AI turns his body inside out, killing him and covering Carl, Donut, and Lexus in his remains. Gamori leaves, and a shaken Lexus 
tells Carl and Donut that their interview has just broken the show's ratings records. Carl's Joey costume still makes it difficult to reach the truck's pedals. So, Glutius Max, one of the dancers from the Desperado 
Club, is chosen to drive the third race. He did best at Mario Kart, but Carl discovers he has been taking stimulants Samantha found among Rishi's belongings, believing they would help him win. He is now hallucinating, 
and there is no time to set up Donut's driving controls before the race begins. Donut's princess throne upgrade has been installed in the passenger seat. It unfolds into a pet bed designed to protect her in a crash and 
comes with a speaking assistance she names Dota. Carl prepares miniature missiles filled with a special stink bomb mixture to interfere with the other team's vehicles without destroying them. The AI also announces that 
the vehicles will be protected from damage for the first 90 seconds of the race. As they wait to start, thousands of sugar hermits pour onto the road. These creatures wear decorated skulls as shells and feed on brains 
and bones. And their description says they are migrating toward the enormous skull blocking the finish line. One wraps its tentacles around the head of a draconian mercenary hired by one fine pig, but cannot hurt him 
while the opening 90 protection is active. Luca D, one of the crawlers who gave Donut her train hat, contributes a spell called temporary macaroni to her banquet spell book. Luca's note thanks Carl and Donut and tells 
Donut not to blame herself with the choice she faced with war crime back in Faction Wars. Now, as Glutius speeds recklessly into the race, Carl lowers two cages mounted on arms outside the truck. Each carries a hired 
gold worker who can throw potion balls at the other racers. Carl then fires his missiles at the team's one fine pig and team sparkles, coating their protective shields in thick mucus that blocks the driver's views and 
slows their vehicle. Carl uses her shield spell to protect the truck, but the cages remain outside its barrier, leaving the ghouls exposed to the sugar hermits swarming the road. The ghouls throw biscuit packs onto the 
creature's path, and these packets expand into hard foam, crushing some of the sugar hermits and forcing others aside. Now, after their truck passes Team Sparkles, Donut cast wall of fire alongside their own vehicle to 
hold everyone back. The spell's increased level produces a much taller and longer wall than they expect. The AI identifies the enormous skull blocking the finish as em this giant beetle-like creature it says Odet once 
killed. It has borrowed pieces of his corpse from the nothing to be used in the races. Now Sugar Hermits begin raining down on the vehicles and Rapture from the lady dominators kills one of Carl's exposed ghoul workers 
with fire. Donut then uses her new temporary macaroni spell to create enormous pasta tubes that the truck can drive through for shelter. She repeatedly casts a spell to keep themselves protected, though the sugar 
hermits still get through the gaps between the tubes. Carl tries to guide Chiomi into the tunnels, but the system tells him she is already dead. The Wild Hunt and Juggler teams are both eliminated after losing all of 
their members. Carl also loses his remaining goal when a sugar hermit decapitates it as he tries to pull it back into the truck. When Glutius passes out, Carl then grabs the wheel and Donut takes over the accelerator. 
With the giant skull still blocking the finish, Carl leans out of the truck, keeping one hand on the wheel and prepares to smash through it using his daughter's kiss ability. Before he can do that, Dwight fires a 
projectile that knocks Corky's cage aside, clips the Lady Dominator's car, and strikes the skull. The explosion launches all three vehicles across the finish line. Carl's truck breaks apart on landing, but he and Donut 
end up winning the race. Now, because Carl and Donut both helped drive during this race, neither will be allowed to drive in the next one. The next race will take them 99 km through a jungle filled with acid rain, 
traps, and monsters. They have 20 hours to finish, including a required refueling stop in the city of Apano. Several heats will share the course, and some routes will require the teams to complete quests along the way. 
Messages from the other crawlers show that more of them are being forced to race against one another. Ammani and Ellie report that two opposing teams were eliminated in their heat, including a newly arrived crawler 
team, while Zang's opponents are now all crawlers. Carl sends Rosetta and Tippid to hire at least two reliable drivers along with more mercenaries to help defend the truck during the race. With the Joey costume finally 
off, Carl returns to the safe room to recover. Rosetta and Tippid bring in three mercenaries who have already helped other teams finish first and second in earlier races. Olga, a toadlike Grok and Finley, a badger-like 
poor suck with poisonous enchanted claws, can drive, while Kimada, a small fire fairy, will help protect them. When Kimata notices Carl's shrine to Ember, she demands three times the price they had agreed on. Carl badly 
needs the drivers, so he accepts. Kimada explains that Ambress sent her to help Carl complete his quest to kill Helock, the god's own brother. She expects to die in the attempt, so the higher fee she demanded is meant 
to support her mercenary teammates afterward. Carl fears that Empress will kill him if he refuses, but also will punish him for killing Helic if he succeeds. As Carl compares Helic with the other gods he has 
encountered, his thoughts turn to Aerys, the goddess of chaos. She suddenly appears with a robot Uzi Jesus, now her pet, and freezes everyone except Carl. Her presence activates the scavenger's daughter patch on his 
back, randomly making a nearby temporary magical effect permanent. Aerys tells him Ammani will be able to explain the result once she leaves. Aerys then offers to protect Carl from Ember and help him kill Helock if he 
sincerely becomes her worshshiper. In return, he must help her win the ascendancy and allow her to cause destruction on Earth's surface. She claims she can rebuild afterward. Then she produces a coin showing four 
possible disasters. Donut's death, Carl losing his feet, most of his friends dying, or fire devastating the surface. Era says one must happen before the next ascendant is chosen. Carl offers to worship her immediately 
to stop it, but she refuses. When robot Uzi Jesus tosses the coin, Carl catches it and holds on despite its burning heat. Aerys announces that he has chosen a fifth possibility and the coin disappears, leaving a slowly 
turning swirl tattooed on his right palm. She will not tell him whether this means escaping the disasters or facing some combination of them. And even the AI admits it does not understand what she is doing. Ammani 
discovers what changed when Aerys activated Carl's patch. Jacobist, the reverse tooth fairy she normally summons for only a short time, will now remain with her permanently instead of returning to his card. Carl tells 
his friends about Aerys's coin in a disasters she threatened. Propertente compares the situation to the earlier trap that forced them to find a way to save both Donut and Katya and agrees to think about a way out. Carl 
also has ideas for saving his friends, but first wants to question Akuma about his offer of an escape. So Carl brings his friends to meet Akuma despite Akuma's demand that he come alone. Before entering the room where 
the war mage is waiting, Carl disables and takes a disintegration trap hidden on the door. Ellie confronts Akuma about the war mages stealing their gate and attacking her during faction wars. Donut silences him with her 
mute spell while Ellie attacks him with ice magic and demands answers. Ammani prepares an anti-agic shield to prevent him from retaliating when they let him speak. Akuma explains the dungeon has too few NPCs to replace 
all the eliminated racing teams, forcing the organizers to draw on earlier floors and mercenary reserves. Reusing NPCs too many times lets memories of their previous lives break through their assigned identities. He 
credits Herrot, a former crawler Carl recognizes as another cookbook author, with developing the worm path method to help NPCs realize who they are. Akuma claims the awakening is now so widespread that the organizers 
will have to destroy all existing NPCs before the next season. Herroat is trapped in the Pineapple Cabaret, a refuge secretly built by two former crawlers alongside the 17th floor. It occupies a separate pocket 
dimension where NPCs and mobs can survive the collapse of a dungeon floor, but it has no established exit to the surface. Akuma believes the AI's expanding influence may now make such an exit possible. The war mages 
left the cabaret to join faction wars and find the scavenger's daughter, a being whose help along with her fathers they hoped to use to reach the surface. While they were away, the refuge's protection expired and old 
dungeon monsters including awakened shadow mimics overran it. Only five war mages remain, and they need Carl and his allies to help reclaim it. Akuma proposes getting into the cabaret through the Desperado Casino or a 
loophole in the shop system. However, he warns that anyone who worships a god will be killed by a smite on entry, rolling out many of Carl's friends. Even for those who do enter, their eventual escape to the surface 
remains unproven. When Donut presses him about his demand that Carl eliminate two racing teams, Akuma admits he wanted to force Carl into races against his friends, making him desperate enough to cooperate. So, Carl 
punches him. Carl and his friends then leave Akuma behind, agreeing to contact him again before leaving the floor. Propetente and Morai will investigate the proposed shop route to the Pineapple Cabaret while the 
Desperado Club dancers will look into the casino entrance. Tippid remembers Herat from his time as a guide, but warns Carl against trusting the warm mages. He is especially worried about the shadow mimics Akuma 
described. these creatures should copy only a creature's appearance. Yet, Morai's shadow mimic form let him use a reaper's lethal gaze on Rend. So, Tippid believes this is a glitch and warns that similarly dangerous 
mimics may be loose on their current floor. Ammani has hired a fleshmaner to reunite Cunda's two halves, but they still need to find Porky, the half who became a singer. Now, following a lead on the guild for 
performers, Carl and the others visit the Lollipop Bar. Its hidden guild entrance opens only when someone sings a specially marked karaoke song well enough to fill a performance meter into the green. Carl asks Morai for 
a potion to improve their singing, but it will not be ready until after the next race. Donut's singing attempt fails to open the guild's entrance, leaving them to postpone the search for Porky till after that race. Now 
Olga, one of their newly hired mercenaries, takes the wheel for the fourth race. Carl and Donut's truck now has three upgrades. a gyro to keep it from flipping, an electrifiable bubble buddy shield, and tires that can 
change size to handle different terrain. Zev announces that every vehicle in a mount will also receive a survival containment bubble to protect its occupants from hazards such as acid rain. Spells and projectiles can 
pass through this bubble, so the racers still need their own shields against attacks. Under the new rules, losing a vehicle or mount no longer automatically eliminates a team. They can finish on foot, but must bring all 
of their teammates and find their own protection from the environment once their containment bubble is gone. The compulsory refueling stop lasts at least 2 hours, and its vendors sell equipment to survive those hazards. 
The race's winner will receive a key to an eliminated team's garage, potentially gaining supplies or a spare vehicle they can switch to at a future pit stop. The replacement team, Flamingo, consists of Avaldo and 
Felipe, who ride Bruna, a heavily armored six-legged slaughter new that can climb walls. Carl has clashed with Oswaldo before, but now asks him to work with them and spare the other racers so they can help as many 
people escape as possible. Donut lashes out at Asaldo and then admits to Carl that she is scared and has not been herself. And Carl tells her he is scared, too. Now, before the race begins, the truck's navigation system 
recommends a route to Apano, the required refueling stop that should avoid bosses and mandatory quests. Its map cannot reveal traps, however, so Carl cannot tell whether the route is safe. Carl asks Oswaldo about 
memorial crystals, relics that preserve the memories and knowledge of fallen gods. And Avaldo says Tupa, the god he worships, rejected Apito's crystal as corrupted and then also rejected one from Yasalt, the goddess P 
killed during the faction wars. Tupe has given him a quest to find out why the crystals are not working. Oswaldo has already lost friends who crossed Carl's path and fears he will be next. As the racers enter the 
jungle, Team Sparkles attacks the Lady Dominators and Oswaldo's team. Oswaldo's Mount Bruna survives the attack and chases after Team Sparkles. Meanwhile, Olga is driving Carl and Donut's truck, but Rain fogs its 
protective shield and makes the road difficult to see. Kimada, the fairy mercenary hired to protect the truck, panics over the discovery that NPCs have fabricated pasts. And Olga explains that the friend who used to 
calm her died on the previous floor. When Kimatada begs the god Embers to appear, their backup driver, Finley, uses an enchanted claw to put her to sleep. So, Carl and Donut will have to fend off attacks without her 
help. Then a double-decker bus from another heat merges directly ahead of them, blocking the narrow road. It belongs to the Black Congregation, a racing team donut met at the karaoke bar. Ammani messages that her team 
is following close behind, and that a trap has already swallowed another crawler team's mount, killing its riders. Carl shares his route so they can travel together. Cannibals then begin dropping from trees onto the 
truck's shield. Donut brightens her torch spell to reveal them, but the light attracts an even larger swarm. So, she casts astral paw, creating a giant magical paw that now has the cutting power of her radiant claws and 
sweeps away the attackers. The spell lasts only briefly and cannot be used again for 8 hours. While the continuing assault nearly overheats the truck's shields, the trib's chief, Great Rusty, then attacks with a spell 
called soul suck. Carl's mind balance protects him, but Olga's soul is stolen, leaving her unconscious and rapidly losing health. Carl pulls her from the driver's seat so Finley can take over, and Donut kills the chief 
with her magic missiles. Olga's soul then returns and her health stabilizes, but she remains unresponsive and needs a cleric's help. The cannibal chief's death triggers a mandatory quest called Pasty Inferno. Maurice, 
the rival northern tribes chief, must also be killed before any racers on their track can finish. They drive across the river and their electrified shield kills the flying piranhas that are attacking them. At Upano, the 
truck is held at the pit stop for the required 2 hours. The garage door must stay open and the safe room is inaccessible, leaving Hedi exposed while she repairs the vehicle. Jamal has climbed onto the ceiling with his 
new sticky feet and is too frightened to come down. His growing awareness has made him afraid of dying and losing his friends. Donut uses her hover ability to carry him down and then asks him to help protect Hedi. 
Finley carries the unconscious Olga and Kada out to find a healer, telling Carl they are his family and he promised to keep them safe. As he steps onto the road, One Fine Pig's armored vehicle runs him over and then 
reverses over all three mercenaries, killing them. Carl storms into one fine pig's garage and the Tigins fire a cannon shot that hits a neighboring team's bus, drawing its camel-like racers into the fight. The Tigan's 
electrified shield kills one of the camel racers before Donut is able to talk Carl into backing down. The deaths of Olga and Finley leave Carl and Donut without an eligible driver. They themselves cannot drive because 
they drove in the last heat and they are not allowed to hire a replacement at the pit stop. Donut reminds Carl that they have backup plans and they begin to collect their driver's dead bodies along with the dead 
camel-like racer. Now Carl apologizes for losing control, then returns to one fine pig's garage with a plan to kill the tigrant while sparing Penelopey the pig. Donut distracts them by speaking to the pig about leaving 
an unhealthy relationship. And while they watch Donut, Carl plants two copies of the disintegration trap he recovered from Akuma's door, one on either side of their vehicle. He configures each trap to target one of the 
tigans so Penelope should be unharmed even if one of them is carrying her. Carl and Donut leave the traps in place and walk away. Louie brings Carl a bucket of Splooge, the protective secretions sold at the pit stop. 
Propotente explains that drinking Splooge will protect them from environmental hazards for about half an hour, giving them a way to continue on foot if they lose their vehicle. Zev announces that the second half of each 
heat will take place on a randomly assigned course with any unfinished mandatory quests carried over. Carl and Donut are sent to Satan's Water Park where Floren and Lucia will also be racing, but they still have to kill 
Maurice, the Northern Cannibal Tribes chief, before they can finish. Notifications confirm that Carl's traps have killed the Tigrins, eliminating team one fine pig. There is no death notice for Penelopey, so Carl 
believes she is still alive inside their garage. He and Donut need to win the heat to claim a key that'll let them rescue her. Donut uses her second chance ability to reanimate Olga's corpse for 15 minutes, allowing the 
body to drive while Carl gives its spoken instructions. Before the spell expires, they plan to use Clockwork triplicate to create temporary copies of the body to continue driving. Satan's water park belongs to an 
enormous invulnerable hedgehog named Satan who interferes with the racers as they pass by. Through the Book of Boom, a departing crawler leaves Carl Gutter Bumper, a spell that directs an area attack along a chosen 
path. Carl follows directions from Peppe to avoid a trap that would force them into another boss fight, taking the truck up a wall on its spider legs. Donut also reanimates the dead camel as a backup driver. As they 
travel along the wall, the driver's door suddenly opens and the copy of Olga driving falls out onto the road below where a trap door swallows her, leaving the truck moving without anyone at the controls. The truck falls 
from the wall and breaks two spider legs before its gyro turns it upright. The reanimated camel is too large for the driver's seat, and Carl accidentally pushes his marked palm through its rotten chest while trying to 
adjust the seat. The damaged flesh repairs itself around his hand, revealing that the tattoo Aerys left on his palm can heal the reanimated body. Now, once the camel is driving, Carl casts gutter bumper along the river, 
and Donut follows with Iceelick. The combined spell creates a frozen road that follows the river's curves and reaches farther than Icelick would on its own. Carl then lowers a bundle of spare weapons chained to the back 
of the truck, dragging them across the ice to cut through their pursuing enemies. Donut then cast summon ye vermin, drawing the parks rodents toward her. Swarms of zipper shrews, whose snouts work like drills, tear 
through enemies on their way to the truck and kill Maurice, the cannibal chief, before he can finish casting a spell. With the mandatory quest complete, Carl and Donut can head for the finish. Ahead, Floren attacks Team 
Sparkles, but Satan headbutts a loop in the track and sends both teams vehicles tumbling. Donut summoning spell also attracts Lucine, the rodent member of Team Sparkles, drawing her away from her vine mount and onto 
Carl's truck. The air is poisoning her outside her mount's protections, but she remains under the spell's influence, clinging to the truck and pounding on its windshield. She is still separated from her own team in 
mount when Carl's truck reaches the finish where the barrier does not allow her to pass and so kills her. After the race, Lucia Mar tells Carl that a water goddess is with her and is spreading a promise that children 
will be safe on the 12th floor. She says beings from throughout the dungeon are gathering for the ascendancy. Lucia suddenly begins speaking as a frightened child who recognizes Gutter Bumper as the spell her father 
gave Carl and says her sister is there too. Carl doesn't understand how the children are connected to Lucia. Floren records their names while the child warns that a man keeps killing the children and that people are 
coming to take their bodies. Lucia runs away before they can learn more. The official results confirm that Carl and Donut won the Heat. One fine pig is the only team eliminated. For the next race, they will have 30 
minutes to cross 20 kilometers of an industrial course with extreme heat, upside down tracks, and gaps up to a 100 m wide. Teams will also be able to steal one another's protective containment bubbles. If their vehicle 
remains in contact for more than 5 seconds, one may lose its protection when they pull apart. Meanwhile, Tran reports that his team won after Zang let him pass, but Lina used her dread ability to make other racers kill 
one another. Only five of the 24 teams in their heat survived. A flashback reveals that the man visiting Ellie as her fan, Lionus, is actually his brother, Minus. Just before the 10th floor began, syndicate security 
killed the real Lionus and recruited Minus to take his place. He is given Lionus' fan posts, hundreds of hours of footage of Ellie, and injected memories to prepare him to fool the AI. Linus is ordered to kill a 
crawler. Tourists are normally prevented from attacking crawlers, but the impersonation may let him slip past the AI's restrictions. Other agents are already in place, including some among the crawlers. Their aim is to 
disrupt the crawl and force an early ascendancy while security tries to contain the AI's spread. Winning the race earns Carl and Donut a garage key and a choice of upgrades. Carl plans to use the key to rescue Penelopey 
from one fine pig's garage for their vehicle upgrade. They choose a stronger bubble buddy shield and booster rockets to help cross the next course's wide gaps, a heat sink to prevent overheating, and golden roller 
limbbo which lets the vehicle flatten itself to slide through narrow openings. Samantha recognizes the scent of the goddess Lucia mentioned on Carl and calls her Chachi. She warns that Chachi claims to protect children, 
but has sacrificed them or allowed them to be killed when it suited her. After hearing Azra speak through Lucia, Carl is alarmed by the possibility that this goddess is with the children inside Lucia's head. Rosetta 
describes Chachi as a minor unsponsored goddess associated with childbirth and water. Morai says he killed her during an earlier crawl, but cannot explain what is happening now with Lucia. Donut plans to sing a duet 
with Carl at the Lollipop Bar using potions and scrolls to improve Carl's voice. They hope that a successful performance will open the hidden performers guild where Porky may be waiting. Before returning to the bar, 
Carl uses the garage key to find Penelopey alive in one fine pig's abandoned garage and brings her out. At the bar, Carl meets Gregori the placid, the fleshmancer hired to reunite Corki and Porky. Zang tells him that he 
plans to kill his team's mount, believing this will kill him both and Lee Na. Carl explains though that the new rules have removed that automatic penalty. Lea could survive without the mount, so Zang would die without 
having stopped her. Zang still loves her, but feels helpless, revealing that she replaced one of her own eyes with her dead brothers. Carl proposes sending Lena to the Pineapple Cabaret instead. Lena may be able to 
enter the cabaret because she cannot worship a god and Bautista could then race with Zang in her place. The dancers Carl hired from the Desperado Club report that its casino games no longer offer passage into the 
nothing, closing that possible route to the Pineapple Cabaret. Morai reports that an early test of the Cleanerbot plan worked on NPCs, but the full journey remains untested. Herat, the former crawler trapped in the 
cabaret, has placed a standing order to buy cleaner bots, and Carl hopes to hide people inside the bots and use the purchases to have the shop system deliver them to the cabaret. Manurva, a former crawler trapped there 
after supervising NPC training on the 17th floor, still has access to a shop interface inside as well. They cannot test that final transfer without committing a bot to the sale. The cabaret is infested with ogres and 
shadow mimics, so getting there will not end the danger. Even so, it could offer Lea a chance to survive. Her left to fester poison will worsen when the next floor's stairs restore her health while entering the 
pineapple cabaret might avoid having that effect. The war mages also claim there may be a way from the cabaret to Earth's surface where she could seek a cure. Carl decides to explain the risks and let Lee Na choose 
whether to try the transfer before they send anyone else. While Carl and Donut prepare for their karaoke performance, Ellie, Zen, and Tran go to explain the cabaret plan to Lee Na. Now, for karaoke, each singer will 
receive a separate score, so either could earn access to the hidden performers guild. Carl takes potions that help him sing in tune and sustain notes, and then uses a scroll to reach the song's high notes. Dong arrives 
at the crowded bar carrying his enormous sock despite being told to stay out of trouble. As Carl and Donut begin their duet, a drunken Dwight attacks the DJ with his horn. The DJ dies, but the music keeps on playing. 
Dwight blames Carl and Donut for Lucine's death, and his attack turns into a brawl among the racers. Carl and Donut keep singing, afraid that stopping now will cost them their last chance to enter the guild. With the DJ 
now dead, their friends try to protect the other racing team since more deaths could bring replacement crawlers into the next heat and donut casts Icelick to disrupt the fighting. But a mantis-like attacker cuts open 
Dong sock spilling coins and nearby NPCs are grabbing them and walking away. Carl does end up earning a high enough score to pass the singing test, but another racer falls into donut and interrupts her last line, 
causing her to fail. The bar's secret door opens for Carl, giving him permanent access to the stage performance guild. Though unfortunately, Donut cannot enter with him. Dong's sock mends its tear, but stays much 
smaller even as his friends try to recover as many coins as they can. Jurgen begs Carl to send him through the Pineapple Cabaret so he can find his wife Heidi, who has stopped answering him. Carl explains that Jurgen's 
worship of a god could make entering the Pineapple Cabaret fatal. Jurgen asks whether a willing god could help him around that restriction, but Carl does not know and can only promise to keep trying. Inside the guild, 
Carl finds Porky, Cunda's missing half. Carl offers to break Porky out and have the fleshmaner reunite the two halves. Porky agrees to have him save him, but also wants Carl's help punishing Dong, who he blames for 
their predicament. Splash Zone, Glutius, and Dr. Bones have disappeared after going to see the leader of the Guild of Suffering. The system says they are no longer on the floor, but their mercenary contracts are still 
charging him, and there are no death notices. Carl warns Bucket Boy not to follow them while their fate remains unknown. Dong's health begins falling under a curse called negative ROI. Moreai says the intelligent being 
inhabiting the sock has moved on, and they need every stolen coin back to stop the curse. With the coins scattered among fleeing NPCs, Carl sends Ammani to help Dong and prepares to rescue Corki during the race. Bigs, 
one of the sluggalos, confronts Carl for keeping Dong away from Corki and treating his relationship as an obstacle. Carl realizes he has been focused on completing the quest instead of helping his friend. So, he 
apologizes and promises to take Dong, Porky, and Gregori onto the race so they can attempt the reunion together. Morai explains that with Lee Na's permission, they will put her inside a modified pet carrier that a 
cleanerbot must swallow before it breaks open after 10 seconds. Unlike ordinary inventories, the bot's storage can hold the occupied carrier. They will then deactivate and sell the bot through Herro's standing order, 
though they cannot guarantee Lina will reach the cabaret safely or remain safe when the four collapses. Donut names the bot Sakira. And since ordinary messages may not reach Lena afterward, Rosetta gives Carl a cactus 
carrying one of Lena's dread traps. Its glow and condition will help them distinguish whether she is still alive, dead, still in storage, or physically outside of the dungeon. Lena can also remotely make a single flower 
bloom while the trap remains glowing to signal that it is safe for others to follow her. Donut receives big ass magnet through her spell book, a spell that turns an object into a powerful magnet. Carl drives into the 
fifth heat with Dong and Porky and Gregori strapped into the new rear seats. Though Dong's health is still falling, they have chosen Gregori the fleshmaner as their backup driver, but he has had no time to learn the 
controls. Racers from 12 heat, including Prepente and Jurgen, enter a factory course that takes them along walls, ceilings, and above molten metal. And Carl follows the Dominators because their upgraded navigation 
system has more information about the course than his. So, Carl follows the Dominators over conveyor belts and loose metal spheres until they reach a gap nearly 90 m wide. Their upgraded bubble buddy shield lets the 
truck glide, and Carl fires the booster rockets to carry it across. They almost missed, but luckily they make it and correct their course. Now, the racers then crash into piles of white powder, filling the factory with 
cocaine dust and incapacitating the small workers there, called knockers. The AI's description warns that the magically created security can still attack, even if the workers cannot. The powder makes Prepente's bat, 
Bianca, too ill to retrieve Corki, forcing him to withdraw. Carl finds the Dominator's car wrecked at the bottom of a hidden hole among crates of toys. Its protective containment is gone and the powder has incapacitated 
Genesis Rapture and Corki inside while animated dolls begin to tear the car apart. Donut jumps down and uses Puddle Jumper to bring Corki out. The racing rules though prevent her from teleporting Corki directly into the 
truck. So, she lands beside it and Carl gets out to carry him on board through the intense heat. A tiny doll then melts into Corky's containment suit and pulling it away tears a larger hole, exposing his organs. Gagori 
takes over driving while Carl tents the Corki. Though, when Gregori becomes too motion sick to continue, Dong takes the wheel until Carl can return back to the controls. The attacking dolls and toy soldiers have 
absorbed infusion magic leaking through the factory, which lets them pass through the truck's shields. Gagori clears the drugs effects from Corki and prepares to reunite him and Porky, but must first remove the suits, 
keeping their organs in place. Carl drives up the factory wall and onto the ceiling above the molten metal. Inside the upside down truck, Gregori removes Corki and Porky's containment suits and begins to join their 
bodies. Dong and Donut support their exposed organs and hold the halves together while Carl tries to keep the truck steady. Despite his own failing health, Dong keeps holding the halves in place until their brain and 
hearts join. Their separate health bars merge and the names Corki and Porky are replaced by Cunda. A divine death mark then appears over Cunda and Gro, the god he worships, enters the realm. The Maestro, the god 
sponsor, uses the god to attack Carl. Carl then drives off the ceiling and uses Bubble Buddy and the rockets to glide, but a blow overwhelms the shield and damages one of the tires. Donut, however, uses laundry day to 
eject the Maestro from Gro's body, and he falls into the molten metal. Freed from the Mestro's control, Gro speaks for himself and condemns Corkca for the years he spent divided into Corki and Porky. Cunda had hoped 
that becoming whole again would satisfy his god, but realizes he is still marked for death. With the exit blocked and regenerating slag elementals closing in, Kunda embraces Dong and offers to carry him into one last 
battle. Dong takes out his big lance Carl gave him and donut enchants it with the big ass magnet spell. Its pull begins immediately and grows stronger over 15 seconds, so they must quickly get out of the truck. Dong 
rides Corunda out to charge Gro. The lance draws screws and other metal towards them, tearing apart the slag elementals and clearing a path for their friends. The flying metal also strikes Dong as he lowers his lance 
toward the god. Both he and Cunda die in the charge. Gro calls it a good death and leaves. While Carl's truck escapes through the magically opened hole and crosses the finish line with 15 seconds remaining. The final 
two races will take place inside an apartment building. The racers will be shrunk, so more than 300 heats will be able to fit inside. In the sixth race, they'll have two hours to reach the bottom from the top, choosing 
routes and completing tasks along the way. A mandatory 2-hour pit stop will follow, but they will not have access to their safe rooms during that time. The AI admits it does not fully understand the cabaret and other 
spaces connected to the dungeon or everything the scavenger's daughter has done. It does, however, warn Carl about exits that seem too easy. Then Morai reports a single flower blooming on the cactus which was Leon's 
signal that she reached the cabaret and considers it safe for the others to follow. Bucket boy, Bigs, and Samantha return expecting to see Dong and Cunda, leaving Carl and Donut to explain that they have lost them both. 
Cascadia then announces that only one team in each heat of three will survive the final race. If a teammate takes an exit deal, the remaining members still must finish the race. Carl and his friends meet in the advanced 
pet stables where Rosetta says a bug prevents the gods from seeing or hearing them. About 200 crawlers have volunteered to leave through the cabaret, while roughly 1,500 plan to take exit deals. Carl plans to leave his 
party temporarily on the 11th floor to keep Donut from being caught in the danger he's preparing to unleash. And he has written an explanation in the book of Boom and now asks Rosetta what she knows about the 
scavenger's daughter. Rosetta describes conflicting myths about older gods overthrown by the current pantheon and banished into the nothing shiel. In one version, Nabbett is a vulture-like goddess of life and protection 
whose children include a pito and a centipede. Other versions identify Scolopendra as the scavenger or describe the daughter as the first mortal. The stories disagree about her origins but repeatedly give the daughter 
the power to overthrow the gods and replace them. A prepente shows Carl Apito's memorial crystal which remains empty despite attempts to charge it through kills. Alvaldo could not make it work either, though it vibrated 
when Urillo, a god banished into the nothing, appeared after faction wars. Propetente has kept it because the midnight epicure, the god he worships, ordered him to obtain it at the start of the butcher masquerade and 
hold it until he knew how to use it. He describes the Midnight Epicure as an apocalyptic god that will destroy existence and return the creatures it has consumed to the galaxy. When Samantha overhears their discussion, 
Donut tells her that Carl plans to leave their party, summon immortals who hate one another, and get them to kill each other despite the rules meant to prevent it. About 200 crawlers preparing to leave for the pineapple 
cabaret gather in hungry eyes to say goodbye to the friends staying behind. Bautista, Zang, Tran, and Archie are among those planning to go, and Morcai's assessment has cleared some crawlers with animal forms to join 
them. Batista serves tea, giving the racers who are staying a blend that strengthens their vehicles and mounts. In his farewell, he speaks about how much serving his friends has meant to him, and asks them to remember 
him. The man posing as Lionus helps hand out cups. Carl and Ellie address the departing crawlers with Ellie remembering her late husband Barry and the friends who have become her new family. She then turns to the guy 
claiming to be Lionus and reads from a private passage in which the real Lionus described finding the same sense of belonging among the fans. His friend shared the correspondence over the Princess Posi board, helping 
Carl's group discover that the visitor was an impostor. The visitor admits that his name is Minus, Lionus's brother, and says security recruited him after Lionus was already dead. He was sent to kill Louis and Ammani in 
the hope that their deaths would turn the surviving crawlers against one another. Unable to attack Minus because of his tourist protection, Carl sends him back to his orbiting ship with a warning that friends will be 
waiting for him there. Ammani reports that 227 crawlers have departed inside the cleaner bots sold through the shop system in addition to Lina. A plant is linked to each crawler and will wilt or turn to dust if they die 
and bloom if they leave the dungeon, though they can't confirm if they've reached safety. Pontiff, one five pig's former driver drives the sixth race accompanied by Netor, a hired cgrapher whose radar and gravity spells 
can help them navigate. Their new upgrade chosen by the audience gives the truck's navigation system a hologram of Dr. Metaf Bee's therapist and control of the vehicle's diagnostics. Dr. Metaf promptly silences Dorado, 
the assistant built into Donut's protective seat, and disables the seat for several hours, leaving Donut without its protection. They begin inside an air duct on the seventh floor of the apartment building. To reach the 
finish, they must drive through a ring on each floor. So, Carl cannot simply take a shortcut straight down the lobby. All the floors will allow a choice of apartments, except that their team must visit apartment number 
231 on the second floor. They emerge from the air duct into an apartment occupied by artificial people labeled as human shells. Their eyes are sewn shut and eyes in the photographs and television images have been 
crossed out except those in a picture of a younger tr. Other racers report finding homes connected to their own families. Tippid warns Carl not to kill the shells which may have creatures hidden inside them. After 
clearing the first ring, Donut uses her whole spell to reach the next apartment down where they pass through the next ring. When Floren reports finding a version of Lucia Maher in her father's house, the AI pauses the 
race and explains that these apartments show how the crawlers lives might have turned out differently using imitations of real people. As they clear the ring on the fourth floor, the human shells begin to pull at the 
stitches over their eyes and their bodies begin to come apart. The next apartment shows an exhausted Ammani coming home to relatives and Carl warns the real Ammani and Ellie who are headed for the same room. As he 
approaches the ring, one of the human shells burst open with beetles coming out of them. The AI explains that these are invulnerable sacred feast scarabs that came from Kefrey's temple and were meant to form a boss on 
the roof, but contact with Carl's blessed foot triggered their attack early. Kefrey has moved away from where the AI expected him to be, preventing it from controlling the swarm. So, it cancels the boss fight, but 
leaves the Beatles invulnerable. Donut opens a hole through the floor so Carl's team and Ammani and Ellie's team can escape the scarabs. Now in apartment 231, we see Marjorie, the owner of Ferdinand, afraid to report 
her abusive partner for violating a restraining order because he might lose his job. The scene reminds Carl and Donut of a visit when Bee called the police to help her. Carl recalls Bee explaining that Marjorie blamed 
herself for the abuse and regrets having judged her. They find the real ring among the traps and drive through it. Jurgen asks Carl to help Prepente, who is refusing to leave an apartment containing an imitation of 
Miriam Dom. With Ovaldo claiming to be near the finish, Carl fears the delay will leave his team in last place. So Carl detonates a bomb hidden in Team Free Love's cooler, killing Ryoslav and Yasha, the bug bears he 
rescued in the first race. While Samantha distracted them earlier, he used Uzi form to slip inside and replace a peach beer with the explosive. Their elimination means Carl's team will survive, even if they finish last, 
giving him time to help Prepente. After clearing the seventh ring, Carl drinks Splooge to survive the toxic air outside the truck and goes to find Prepente. Propertente is sitting beside the imitation of Miriam as she 
plays piano in a luxurious New York apartment, imagining the career she might have had if she had not stayed home to care for her parents. In that life, she would have never had known him. And he feels so unwanted by 
his own friends that he wishes he had never eaten the biscuit that changed him. Carl reminds Prepotente that the room shows only an imagined life while the real Miriam had people and animals who loved her and assures 
him that their friends want him around. When Donut and Jurgen arrive and the room starts breaking apart, Prepente embraces Carl and lets him carry him back to the truck and allows him to finally call him Pony. Carl and 
Donut finished second behind team sparkles, passing Free Love's wreck just short of the finish, where the Bug Bears had been moments away from surviving. When Oswaldo arrives third with about a minute left, Carl learns 
that he lied about being near the exit. Believing that lie led Carl to sacrifice the bug bears, which saved Oswaldo from elimination, the Outreach Guild opens during the final pit stop for crawlers who want to leave 
through exit deals. Fewer than a thousand crawlers remain after the apartment race, and they learned that NPC teams were not required to visit specific apartments, giving them an advantage over the crawlers. An 
announcer named Damian encourages them to accept the deals and warns against the unauthorized Pineapple Cabaret. He explains that the winning teams will take their garages and hired NPCs to the 11th floor, provided 
those NPCs are inside a garage or vehicle when they descend. The survivors will then have 90 minutes to build parade floats around assigned themes using the resources they already have. While their allies steal upgrades 
from eliminated team's garages, Carl prepares his tower of power, a vertical chain of explosives intended to blast a route through the apartment building. Hedi upgrades the truck's rocket so they can launch it all the 
way up to the roof and steer during the flight. Now, of the 989 remaining crawlers, 715 plan to leave and take exit deals. Louis, Britney, Floren, Lucia Mar, Ammani, and Ellie, though choose to continue. Carl expects to 
race Team Sparkles and Oswaldo, while Ammani and Ellie expect a Russian crawler team in the MPC team called the Black Congregation. When speaking to Carl, Britney trembles and presses her hand against his chest. He 
hears her voice inside his mind telling him not to worry about her and to focus on surviving. He feels a strange connection between them, but does not understand it. Pontiff reports another possible escape route through 
the casino. The wheel no longer offers its former entrance to the cabaret, but a new option marked nothing might send travelers to a holding area outside the playing field where Herro could retrieve them. Jamal then 
joins Carl and Donut for the final race carrying a flamethrower to help defend the truck. At the starting line, they discover that the crawler teams have been rearranged. Ammani and Ellie must race Chris, while Louis 
and Britney face Floren and Lucia Mah. Even though some heats contain only NPC teams, Carl's friends must race against each other with only one team in each heat allowed to survive. As Carl protests the forced matchups, 
the AI then announces that Scholar Pendra's nine-tier attack has begun and threatens most of the dungeon, including the floors where the crawlers are. The nine attacks will initially be at least 3 hours apart with less 
predictable intervals later. The first attack randomly transforms one and five unprotected targets. Donut, Jamal, and Samantha, who had been stowed away in the truck, escaped its effects, but Carl becomes transformed 
into a long-haired dashhound with a German accent, and his name Carl is now spelled with a K. His equipment shifts. Some items return to his inventory, and his usable abilities change with his body. NPCs and other 
affected people will remain transformed for 6 hours, while crawlers must pass through a stairwell to recover their original forms. The race still begins in two minutes, leaving Carl suddenly unable to drive as planned. 
Carl registers Samantha as a mercenary and assigns her to steer while Donut handles the pedals. Ammani reports that the attack has turned Ellie into a goblin and her permanent card summoned Jacobus into a starfish. 
Chris has become a werewolf, though in human form. Prepetente and Jurgen both received protection notices leading Prepotente to believe that Apito's memorial crystal can shield everyone on his mount from the Scholar 
Pendra attacks. Now, when the race begins, Dr. Metaf coordinates shots that pierce Team Sparkle's shield, poison its living vine mount, and disables its navigation system. Donut turns to smoke to reach Dwight, and then 
cuts off his head with her claw, eliminating their team. Carl detonates the tower of power. His vertical chain of explosives blasting a passage through the building to the roof portals. Oswaldo, who's competing in 
